<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends marginally weaker vs dollar.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends marginally weaker vs dollar.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed marginally weaker at 43.2960/2990 to the dollar in interbank trading on Wednesday compared to the previous close of 43.2950/2980.</p>
<p>Dealers said the local unit was quoted at 43.2940/2990 per dollar in early trade but slipped slightly later on buying of the U.S. currency by importers.</p>
<p>Call money was traded at Tuesday's level of 5-6 percent, they added.</p>
<p>--Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
</text>
